From: CodeAndSolder <codeandsolder@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uclient: annotate intentional partial response fallthrough

When resuming HTTP downloads, the successful 206 Content-Range validation
must then pass into the common 200/204 response handling. An ordinary
comment is not recognized under strict -Wimplicit-fallthrough=5.

Keep the response semantics and mark the shared-code branch explicitly.

---
--- a/uclient-fetch.c
+++ b/uclient-fetch.c
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@
 			request_done(cl);
 			break;
 		}
-		/* fall through */
+		__attribute__((__fallthrough__));
 	case 204:
 	case 200:
 		if (no_output)
